---
source: crates/acpilot-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: stdout(&top)
---
Edit and run ACP agents over one daemon

Usage: acpilot [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  version    Print version and protocol information
  ext        Install, verify, and approve extensions
  secret     Store, list, and remove credentials in the OS keyring
  token      Show and rotate the token a TCP daemon requires
  config     Explain which settings file a value came from
  profile    Create, inspect, and remove profiles
  workspace  Open, list, and remove workspaces
  tui        Open the terminal UI against a running daemon, or run one here
  serve      Serve the daemon and the web UI over HTTP, printing its address and token
  doctor     Report what this machine has, and what a project is missing
  models     Probe a declared model server, and print what it answered
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --profile <NAME|DIR>
          Profile name, or a profile directory.
          
          Accepted before or after the subcommand, because every verb that has an opinion about
          identity reads one choice. A single segment is a profile name under `<config>/profiles`; a
          path opens that directory. `tui` and `serve` use it only when they start the daemon: a
          daemon already running keeps the profile it was started with, and naming a different one
          there is an error rather than a silent mismatch. A name that does not resolve is an error,
          never a quieter fallback: guessing sends a work prompt with a personal key.
          
          [env: ACPILOT_PROFILE=]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
